.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-1.txt:32:O blast radius concreto é refresh de hooks/scripts/skills/agentes/schemas, merge de settings e `.env`, seis rotas `docs/.github`, regravação de manifesto/estado e possível refresh de harness. Sem as condições, o resultado pode ser posse indevida ou sobrescrita de arquivo autoral, escrita fora do alvo por links, árvore parcialmente atualizada ou postura bloqueante inesperada no perfil `user`.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-3.txt:34:- **P2 — `templates/.github/workflows/benchmarks.yml.template:119-122`, `:127-133`**: output names use only the benchmark basename. Two skills containing `benchmarks/regression.yaml` overwrite each other’s JSON and Markdown, leaving misleading artifacts even though the aggregate failure flag survives. Derive a collision-free name from the relative path.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-ga/verdict-ga-4.txt:26:   **Minimal fix:** Align current-framework declarations in SPEC, or remove volatile mirrors and reference root `VERSION`; add all such sites to the release-version drift check.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-ga/verdict-ga-4.txt:32:   **Concrete failure scenario:** The GA documentation still calls the artifact an rc/pre-release, says every P1 must be cured before GA, calls migration a pre-GA follow-up, and says the seven VETO-skill migration “lands before GA.” It did not. A v1.3.0 adopter trusting this text can upgrade normally and retain all seven VETO-bearing skills as `name-only`, as condition 2 warns. The npm README likewise limits the unsupported `user` plus Codex/Grok composition to “this rc,” although it remains unsupported in GA.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-ga/verdict-ga-1.txt:21:O upgrade copy-mode atualiza hooks, scripts, commands, skills, agentes, schemas, `SPEC/v1`, marker e settings; entrega seis rotas em `docs/`/`.github/`; regrava manifesto/install-state; e pode atualizar o harness.

